<title>GERMANY: Preussag chief to leave for WestLB - report.</title>
<headline>Preussag chief to leave for WestLB - report.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of diversified metals and engineering group Preussag AG Michael Frenzel is to leave the company and join the board of Westdeutsche Landesbank (WestLB), a German newspaper reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>According to the Welt am Sonntag, Frenzel will join WestLB with the understanding that he will replace the bank's chairman Friedel Neuber when he retires in three years.</p>
<p>Frenzel worked at WestLB between 1981 and 1988 and worked closely with Neuber, who is chairman of Preussag's supervisory board, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
